      "claim": "L6 azosemide hepatic microsome records show low intrinsic clearance in rat liver microsomes (2.70 ± 0.185 ×10^-3 ml/min in controls; 3.60 ± 0.313 µL/min/mg for M1 formation), indicating that the sulfamoyl-chlorophenyl diuretic scaffold is not associated with high hepatic intrinsic clearance.",
