    {
      "claim": "L6 furosemide O-glucuronidation in mouse liver microsomes (CLint 2.47 µL/min/mg) is reported as 5-fold higher than human microsomes, implying low human hepatic intrinsic clearance for this sulfonamide diuretic and supporting limited presystemic hepatic loss for the query's sulfonamide-chlorophenyl motif.",
      "card_ids": ["C254"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 bumetanide record shows no CYP2E1-mediated metabolism and essentially unchanged non-renal clearance after isoniazid pretreatment (2.47 vs 2.22 mL/min/kg), supporting low hepatic clearance in a related sulfonamide diuretic.",
      "card_ids": ["C279"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 indapamide records identify CYP3A4/CYP2C19 as metabolizing enzymes but do not quantify high clearance; combined with L5 rat jejunal permeability for indapamide (Papp 2.18 ± 0.93 ×10^-6 cm/s), the related sulfonamide-chlorophenyl class can be absorbed and is not affirmatively shown to undergo extensive first-pass loss.",
      "card_ids": ["C248", "C259", "C206", "C234"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No L6 record directly measures chlorthalidone; the new hepatic-clearance evidence is directionally supportive and provides no affirmative evidence for F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C258", "C254", "C279"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C258", "C261", "C254", "C279", "C248", "C259"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral-bioavailability record for chlorthalidone is supplied.",
    "No matched oral-versus-IV AUC or absolute F measurement for the query is available.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability data; L6 records are for azosemide, furosemide, bumetanide, indapamide, and other molecules.",
    "Species and assay-system differences (rat/mouse microsomes vs human) limit quantitative transfer.",
    "Dose, formulation, and prandial state for the query are unspecified.",
    "No direct gut-wall efflux or intestinal metabolism data for the query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high. L6 hepatic-clearance records for related sulfonamide-chlorophenyl diuretics (azosemide, furosemide, bumetanide, indapamide) show low-to-modest intrinsic hepatic clearance and no affirmative high first-pass evidence; combined with the favorable neutral, low-MW, moderate-logD physicochemical prior and measurable permeability/exposure in related analogs, F≥20% remains better supported. Confidence stays moderate because all evidence is indirect and no direct query-specific F measurement is available."
}

